  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on identifying 'probable' outcomes (based on a threshold of 1/n) and averaging them. In this case, only the 0 Euro outcomes qualify as probable in both lotteries, leading to an average of 0 for both. However, the individual does not mention or use such a threshold-based filtering of outcomes. They do not compute averages of selected outcomes based on probability thresholds. Instead, they emphasize the multiplicity of winning options in A (i.e., two non-zero outcomes), which increases perceived attractiveness, even though one of these has low value. This reasoning is qualitative and based on the count of favorable outcomes, not on averaging outcomes that exceed a formal probability cutoff. There is no indication that the individual filtered outcomes using 1/n as a criterion or computed averages of such filtered outcomes. Their focus is on the presence of multiple wins and emotional responses (excitement, hope), not on a systematic rule involving probability thresholds and averaging. Therefore, the reasoning mechanism of the decision reason is not reflected in the verbal report.",
